1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:02,167
Mum hid the cookies on top of the fridge.

2
00:00:02,316 --> 00:00:03,328
Grow.

3
00:00:03,368 --> 00:00:04,597
Snack time.

4
00:00:04,797 --> 00:00:05,933
Late for school?

5
00:00:06,253 --> 00:00:06,786
Grow.

6
00:00:06,826 --> 00:00:08,086
One giant step.

7
00:00:08,286 --> 00:00:10,149
Your best friend is looking for you.

8
00:00:10,349 --> 00:00:11,346
Grow.

9
00:00:11,546 --> 00:00:12,620
Again.

10
00:00:12,820 --> 00:00:13,925
Again.

11
00:00:14,125 --> 00:00:16,303
Okay, that's terrifying.

12
00:00:16,634 --> 00:00:19,169
What if you could grow,
any time you wanted?

13
00:00:19,269 --> 00:00:21,349
One word, and you get bigger.

14
00:00:21,549 --> 00:00:22,840
As big as you like.

15
00:00:22,940 --> 00:00:23,968
Sounds amazing.

16
00:00:24,055 --> 00:00:25,300
Pigeons think you're a building.

17
00:00:25,340 --> 00:00:27,405
Your best friend gets
the best seat in town.

18
00:00:27,445 --> 00:00:29,324
And you're the coolest kid in the city.

19
00:00:29,574 --> 00:00:31,237
But here's the catch.

20
00:00:31,277 --> 00:00:34,116
Ten times taller means
a thousand times heavier.

21
00:00:34,156 --> 00:00:35,169
Your bones?

22
00:00:35,209 --> 00:00:37,181
Only a hundred times stronger.

23
00:00:37,221 --> 00:00:40,462
So every square inch of bone
carries ten times the load.

24
00:00:40,662 --> 00:00:44,043
And a human thigh bone breaks at
about ten times your body weight.

25
00:00:44,083 --> 00:00:45,374
Your very first step?

26
00:00:45,554 --> 00:00:46,210
Snap.

27
00:00:46,410 --> 00:00:47,252
That's real.

28
00:00:47,402 --> 00:00:50,658
You sit down on a rooftop
and wait to shrink back.

29
00:00:50,998 --> 00:00:54,446
The next morning, a man in a suit
is waiting in your kitchen.

30
00:00:54,564 --> 00:00:55,824
He has a photo of you.

31
00:00:56,024 --> 00:00:56,959
And an offer.

32
00:00:57,109 --> 00:00:59,003
Then the ceiling starts to crack.

33
00:00:59,203 --> 00:01:02,265
Upstairs, your little
sister just said the word.

34
00:01:02,365 --> 00:01:03,733
Do you run up and save her…

35
00:01:03,836 --> 00:01:04,972
or do you keep your secret?

36
00:01:08,307 --> 00:01:09,567
You run.

37
00:01:09,700 --> 00:01:11,688
Crutch first, every stair.

38
00:01:11,728 --> 00:01:13,390
Her door won't open.

39
00:01:13,590 --> 00:01:15,717
Because her room isn't a room anymore.

40
00:01:15,967 --> 00:01:18,434
Your little sister is
the size of the house.

41
00:01:18,634 --> 00:01:19,646
And she loves it.

42
00:01:19,846 --> 00:01:22,686
She laughs, and every window
on the street rattles.

43
00:01:22,726 --> 00:01:25,720
Here's what you didn't know:
the word works for anyone who hears it.

44
00:01:25,760 --> 00:01:27,267
She waves at the whole street.

45
00:01:27,447 --> 00:01:28,490
Mum faints.

46
00:01:28,690 --> 00:01:29,532
Twice.

47
00:01:29,732 --> 00:01:32,029
She picks up the cat, very gently.

48
00:01:32,069 --> 00:01:33,051
Then she sways.

49
00:01:33,091 --> 00:01:34,165
Blood is heavy.

50
00:01:34,205 --> 00:01:38,004
At ten times her height, her heart
has to push it ten times higher.

51
00:01:38,204 --> 00:01:41,352
That takes about three times
the pressure her heart can make.

52
00:01:41,552 --> 00:01:45,072
And without blood, a brain
switches off in about ten seconds.

53
00:01:45,128 --> 00:01:45,939
That's real.

54
00:01:46,239 --> 00:01:47,081
Ten seconds.

55
00:01:47,281 --> 00:01:49,330
There's only one way to catch her.

56
00:01:49,530 --> 00:01:50,851
You say the word.

57
00:01:50,907 --> 00:01:52,245
Your leg isn't healed.

58
00:01:52,285 --> 00:01:53,731
You do it anyway.

59
00:01:53,931 --> 00:01:54,758
Nine.

60
00:01:54,958 --> 00:01:55,614
Eight.

61
00:01:55,814 --> 00:01:56,687
You catch her.

62
00:01:56,887 --> 00:01:58,533
Then you both sit down, and wait.

63
00:01:58,733 --> 00:02:00,922
Slowly, the street gets bigger again.

64
00:02:01,210 --> 00:02:03,554
Across the street, the man in
the suit isn't calling for help.

65
00:02:03,594 --> 00:02:04,606
He's filming.

66
00:02:04,806 --> 00:02:05,540
Everything.

67
00:02:05,580 --> 00:02:07,536
The next morning,
there's a card on your pillow.

68
00:02:07,736 --> 00:02:09,244
One word on it.

69
00:02:09,444 --> 00:02:10,704
And it isn't grow.

